  "body": "Hi,\r\n\r\nApologies if this is the wrong place to ask, but https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#matching-a-font-type-pattern has 3 of the 5 fonts without a mime type.\r\n\r\nFor example, the first row specifies the font's mime type `application/vnd.ms-fontobject` given a particular byte and mask. But the 2nd through 4th rows don't appear to show a valid mime type.\r\n\r\nIn those cases, what mime type should be returned? I can guess TrueType and OpenType could both be `application/font-sfnt`, but I don't know about TrueType Collect. Or should we consider these undefined?\r\n\r\nThanks",
